# In-app agents (suggest when possible)

When designing or changing Omniscope UI, **proactively suggest** where an AI agent CTA fits. Prefer integrating agents into the user’s flow over leaving them only on the Agents tab.

## When to propose an agent action

- Screen or row has a **symbol / asset / holding**
- User is about to **decide** (buy/sell, size, risk) or asks “what is this?”
- Copy would otherwise say “learn more” / “research” with no in-app path
- New feature surfaces market context that an agent Run already understands

## How to wire it

- Use [`AgentLaunchIntent`](lib/data/agents/agent_launch.dart): `investigate` (research), `tradeCheck` (intraday), `explainLive` (live balances), `explainPortfolio` (allocation guide), or `paperReview` (practice coach).
- Launch via [`AgentLaunchActions.launch`](lib/features/agents/agent_launch_actions.dart) or [`AgentLaunchButton`](lib/widgets/agent_launch_button.dart) — do not push `AgentChatScreen` with a hard-coded role unless intentional.
- Pass the **symbol**; set `autoRun` through the shared helper so chat runs the Genkit role agent (tools + prompt).
- Mobile-first: one CTA if a single connected agent applies; picker when several; when none connected, call `ShellNavigationController.goToAgents(connectRoleId: …)` so the user lands on Agents with Connect open.
- Brand / shadcn only — no ad-hoc Material menus.

```dart
// ❌ BAD — Agents tab only; asset detail has no path into chat
// (user must retype the symbol in Run)

// ✅ GOOD — context-aware launch
AgentLaunchButton(
  symbol: quote.symbol,
  intent: AgentLaunchIntent.investigate,
)
```

## Do not

- Hand-roll provider HTTPS outside [`GenkitAgentRunner`](lib/data/agents/genkit/genkit_agent_runner.dart) — chat turns go through in-process Genkit `defineAgent` + tools.
- Spawn Python or remote agent workers from Flutter UI.
- Claim live brokerage execution from agent output.
- Invent new agent frameworks per screen — extend intents / role mapping instead.
